{"records":[{"id":"bpcpfns6vb","title":"Global genetic interaction network of a human cell maps conserved principles and informs functional interpretation of gene co-essentiality profiles. Billmann et al.","description":"Deciphering how genes interact within human cells is essential for understanding their functional wiring and the development of targeted therapeutic strategies. In this study, we present a genome-scale map of genetic interactions in the human haploid cell line HAP1, based on CRISPR-based perturbation of ~ 4 million gene pairs. The resulting network comprises ~89,000 high-confidence gene-gene interactions, organizing genes into hierarchical modules corresponding to protein complexes and pathways, biological processes, and cellular compartments, mirroring principles observed in yeast and highlighting the functional architecture of a human cell. This large-scale genetic network complements the DepMap gene co-essentiality network by capturing unique functional information, uncovering roles of previously uncharacterized genes, and identifying molecular determinants of cancer cell line-specific genetic dependencies. This study presents a general data-driven strategy analysis for systematically exploring the roles of genes and their functional connections in human cell lines.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-18T10:15:12.084Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bpcpfns6vb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bpcpfns6vb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Maximilian","last_name":"Billmann","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Costanzo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiang","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Arshia Z.","last_name":"Hassan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mahfuzur","last_name":"Rahman","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kevin R.","last_name":"Brown","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Katherine S.","last_name":"Chan","orc